        "/accounts/{accountId}/orders/{orderId}": {
            "get": {
                "summary": "Get order details",
                "tags": [
                    "Orders"
                ],
                "description": "Retrieve a single order by ID.\n\nReturns `404` for an order that is not a bookable reservation - a change request, an order a change request replaced, a declined request or a voucher - unless you pass `includeNonBookable=true`. Webhooks are emitted for those orders, so if you are following an `order.changeRequested` event you will need the parameter.\n\nPass `includeQuestions=true` for the booking form questions the facility asked and the answers the customer gave. See `includeQuestions`.\n",
                "operationId": "getOrder",
                "security": [
                    {
                        "ApiKeyAuth": []
                    }
                ],
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "accountId",
                        "in": "path",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        },
                        "description": "The account ID"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "orderId",
                        "in": "path",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        },
                        "description": "The order ID"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IncludeNonBookable"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IncludeQuestions"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Order details",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OrderDetailResponse"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "401": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
                    },
                    "429": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/accounts/{accountId}/bookings": {
            "get": {
                "summary": "List bookings",
                "tags": [
                    "Bookings"
                ],
                "description": "One row per pet per day, drawn across every order in the window.\n\n**This is the endpoint to build a day sheet from.** An order returned by `GET /accounts/{accountId}/orders` does not carry its bookings, so a day sheet assembled from that list costs one further request per order - 41 requests for a 40-order day. Here a whole day is one request:\n\n`GET /accounts/{accountId}/bookings?date=2026-09-03`\n\nAdd `includeQuestions=true` and the day's booking form answers come back in the same response, so a feeding chart is one call rather than hundreds.\n\n**Bookings that overlap the window, not bookings that start in it.** A pet three nights into a week's boarding is returned for every day of the stay. That is the same test the facility's own day-scoped screens apply, and it is the mistake `minStartDate=D&maxStartDate=D` invites on the order list - there is no way to express it here.\n\n**A date window is required.** Send `date` for a single day, `minDate` and `maxDate` for a span of up to 31 days, or `orderId` for one reservation. A request with none of the three is a `422` naming the three forms: `bookings` is the largest table an account has, and quietly defaulting to \"today\" would answer a question nobody asked.\n\n**What is here and not on the order endpoint:** `status`, `cancelled`, `isNoShow`, `customerId`, the `order` each booking belongs to resolved inline, and `kennelsOnDate`. **What is deliberately not here:** `kennelAssignments` - see `kennelsOnDate` on the response schema.\n\nBookings on cancelled reservations are held back unless you ask for them, and `addon` and `classes` rows are excluded unless you name one in `type` - those are services scheduled against a reservation rather than a pet occupying a spot, and including them would list every pet twice on a sheet.\n\nRequires `orders:read`. Nothing here is a disclosure the single-order endpoint does not already make; this is the same data in the shape a day sheet needs.\n",
                "operationId": "listBookings",
                "security": [
                    {
                        "ApiKeyAuth": []
                    }
                ],
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "accountId",
                        "in": "path",
                        "required": true,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        },
                        "description": "The account ID"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/BookingDate"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/BookingMinDate"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/BookingMaxDate"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "type",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": [
                                "boarding",
                                "daycare",
                                "facility",
                                "addon",
                                "classes"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "One booking type.\n\nWithout this parameter the list contains `boarding`, `daycare` and `facility` only - the types that put a pet somewhere for a stretch of time, which is what a day sheet means by a booking. `addon` and `classes` rows are services scheduled against a reservation; they share the reservation's pet and dates, so returning them by default would list the same pet several times. Name one here to get it.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "status",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": [
                                "booked",
                                "pending",
                                "request"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "One booking status. All three are returned when this is omitted.\n\n`request` is a reservation the customer has asked for and the facility has not yet confirmed, `pending` is awaiting something the account tracks, `booked` is confirmed. A day sheet usually wants `booked`; a board showing what is coming wants all three.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "petId",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        },
                        "description": "One pet's bookings. Unlike `petId` on the order list, this narrows to that pet's own rows rather than returning whole multi-pet reservations.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "customerId",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        },
                        "description": "Read from the booking's own column rather than its order's, so a booking whose order has since been deleted still matches.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "kennelId",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        },
                        "description": "Bookings occupying this kennel, **including the ones only in it for part of the stay**.\n\nA booking that rotates between kennels carries the first one in `kennelId` and the rest as separate segments, so this matches on both. \"Which pets are in kennel 12 today\" would otherwise omit a pet moved into 12 that morning.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "orderId",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        },
                        "description": "One reservation's bookings. Accepted without a date window, because an order bounds itself - which is what a consumer following an `orderId` out of a webhook has, with no dates to hand.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/BookingIncludeCancelled"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/BookingIncludeQuestions"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "sort",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": [
                                "startDate",
                                "endDate",
                                "petId",
                                "kennelId",
                                "id",
                                "created",
                                "updated"
                            ],
                            "default": "startDate"
                        },
                        "description": "`startDate` and `endDate` sort by date **and** time of day, so arrivals come back in the order they happen.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "order",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": [
                                "asc",
                                "desc"
                            ],
                            "default": "asc"
                        },
                        "description": "Ascending by default, unlike the order list - a day sheet is read from the start of the day downwards.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "perPage",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "minimum": 1,
                            "maximum": 200,
                            "default": 50
                        },
                        "description": "Number of items per page. A facility with more than 200 pets on one day pages through them; the window, not the page size, is what keeps the request bounded.\n"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "page",
                        "in": "query",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer",
                            "minimum": 1,
                            "default": 1
                        },
                        "description": "Page number for pagination"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Bookings list",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PaginatedBookings"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "401": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "No date window was given, the window is longer than 31 days, `date` was combined with `minDate`/`maxDate`, or only one end of the range was sent. The message names the accepted forms, under the `date` key.\n",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "properties": {
                                        "message": {
                                            "type": "string"
                                        },
                                        "errors": {
                                            "type": "object",
                                            "additionalProperties": {
                                                "type": "array",
                                                "items": {
                                                    "type": "string"
                                                }
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                },
                                "example": {
                                    "message": "Validation failed",
                                    "errors": {
                                        "date": [
                                            "A date window is required. Send date=YYYY-MM-DD for one day, minDate and maxDate for a span of up to 31 days, or orderId for a single reservation."
                                        ]
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "429": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/accounts/{accountId}/taxes": {
            "get": {
                "summary": "List taxes",
