        "responses": {
            "Unauthorized": {
                "description": "Unauthorized - invalid or missing authentication",
                "content": {
                    "application/json": {
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                                "message": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "example": {
                            "message": "Unauthorized"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "Forbidden": {
                "description": "Forbidden - no access to this resource",
                "content": {
                    "application/json": {
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                                "message": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "example": {
                            "message": "Forbidden: no access to this account"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "NotFound": {
                "description": "Resource not found",
                "content": {
                    "application/json": {
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                                "message": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "example": {
                            "message": "Resource not found"
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "ValidationError": {
                "description": "Validation error",
                "content": {
                    "application/json": {
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                                "message": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                },
                                "errors": {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "additionalProperties": {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "items": {
                                            "type": "string"
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "example": {
                            "message": "Validation failed",
                            "errors": {
                                "question": [
                                    "The question field is required"
                                ]
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "TooManyRequests": {
                "description": "Too many requests - the client's rate limit has been exceeded. No request was processed, so retrying is always safe.\n\nWait at least `Retry-After` seconds before retrying. See the **Rate limiting** section of the API description for the limit, the bucket it is applied to, and the recommended backoff strategy.\n",
                "headers": {
                    "Retry-After": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/headers/Retry-After"
                    },
                    "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
                    },
                    "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
                    },
                    "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
                    }
                },
                "content": {
                    "application/json": {
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                                "message": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "example": {
                            "message": "Too Many Attempts."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "headers": {
            "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "description": "The maximum number of requests permitted in the current window.",
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "example": 600
                }
            },
            "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "description": "The number of requests still available in the current window. Counts down to `0`, at which point further requests receive `429` until the window resets.\n",
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "example": 594
                }
            },
            "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "description": "Unix timestamp (seconds) at which the current window resets and the full quota becomes available again. Sent only on `429` responses.\n",
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "example": 1787005054
                }
            },
            "Retry-After": {
                "description": "Number of seconds to wait before retrying. Sent only on `429` responses. Use this value as the base of the client's backoff delay rather than a hard-coded interval.\n",
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "example": 60
                }
            }
        }
    },
    "security": [
        {
            "ApiKeyAuth": []
        },
        {
            "ApiKeyAuthAlt": []
        },
        {
            "BearerAuth": []
        }
    ],
    "externalDocs": {
        "url": "https://docs.propetware.com/api",
        "description": "Find more info here"
    },
    "tags": [
        {
            "name": "Authentication",
            "description": "Customer authentication and JWT token management"
        },
        {
            "name": "Accounts",
            "description": "Operations related to accounts"
        },
        {
            "name": "Users",
            "description": "Operations related to staff users. Use these to resolve the `userId` returned against order bookings and other records that identify the staff member who acted.\n"
        },
        {
            "name": "Customers",
            "description": "Operations related to customers"
        },
        {
            "name": "Customer Fields",
            "description": "Operations related to customer form fields (standard and custom)"
        },
        {
            "name": "Pets",
            "description": "Operations related to pets"
        },
        {
            "name": "Pet Fields",
            "description": "Operations related to pet form fields (standard and custom)"
        },
        {
            "name": "Orders",
            "description": "Operations related to orders, and the read-only cancellation reason list an order's `cancellationTypeId` resolves against.\n\n**Reading a day's reservations.** The four date filters on the order list AND together, so every order covering a date `D` - including multi-night boarding that started earlier - is one request: `GET /accounts/{accountId}/orders?maxStartDate=D&minEndDate=D`. Use `minStartDate=D&maxStartDate=D` only when you want *arrivals* on `D`; it omits pets already staying.\n\n**An order in a list does not carry its bookings.** Pets, kennels, times, line items and payments are assembled only by the single-order endpoint, so a day sheet built from the list costs a request per order. Read the `Bookings` tag instead: `GET /accounts/{accountId}/bookings?date=D` is the same day, one row per pet, in one request.\n\nThe reason list is here rather than under its own ability because a cancelled order already carries the reason resolved inline, so `orders:read` covers both.\n"
        },
        {
            "name": "Bookings",
            "description": "One row per pet per day. This is the booking-shaped read of the same data the order endpoints return order-shaped, and it is what a day sheet, a kennel board or a feeding chart should be built from.\n\n`GET /accounts/{accountId}/bookings?date=D` returns every pet present on `D` - including multi-night boarding that started earlier - with its kennel, its times, its staff member and the reservation it belongs to. Add `includeQuestions=true` for the booking form answers in the same response. The equivalent through the order endpoints is one list request plus one request per order.\n\nA date window is required: `date` for a day, `minDate` + `maxDate` for up to 31 days, or `orderId` for a single reservation. Requires `orders:read` - this is not a new disclosure, it is a cheaper shape for one that already exists.\n"
        },
        {
            "name": "Taxes",
            "description": "Operations related to account taxes"
        },
        {
            "name": "Notes",
            "description": "Operations related to customer, pet, and order notes, and the read-only note tag list a note's tags resolve against.\n\nEach list is scoped the way the matching panel in ProPet is scoped, so an integration reading notes sees what staff see. The practical consequence is that notes belonging to a single booking appear on the order-notes list and nowhere else; `bookingId` identifies them.\n\nA note belongs to exactly one of a customer, a pet or an order - ProPet's own note creation writes one scoping column and clears the others when a note is reclassified. So a pet note has `petId` and a null `customerId`; it is not also a customer note, and it does not appear on the customer's list.\n\nThe note tag list is here rather than under its own ability because every note already carries its tags resolved inline, so `notes:read` covers both.\n"
        },
        {
            "name": "Breeds",
            "description": "Operations related to account breed lists"
        },
        {
            "name": "Secondary Pet Statuses",
            "description": "Operations related to custom secondary pet status options"
        },
        {
            "name": "Colour Codes",
            "description": "Operations related to colour code definitions for pets and customers"
        },
        {
            "name": "Vaccinations",
            "description": "Operations related to pet vaccination records"
        },
        {
            "name": "Preventives",
            "description": "Operations related to pet preventive medication records"
        },
        {
            "name": "Documents",
            "description": "Read-only access to the files attached to a pet - vaccination certificates and preventive records. Requires the `documents:read` ability, which is separate from `vaccinations:read`: a key that may read vaccination dates does not automatically get the uploaded paperwork.\n\nUpload is not offered over the API. Files arrive through the account UI.\n"
        },
        {
            "name": "Kennels",
            "description": "Read-only access to the kennels (\"spots\") a facility books pets into, and the kennel types they are grouped under. Requires the `kennels:read` ability, which is separate from `accountSettings:read`: a key that needs to label a kennel on a chart should not have to be granted the whole settings surface to do it.\n\nBookings carry a `kennelId`, and split bookings carry one per date range. These endpoints are how such an id becomes a name. Both lists come back in the order the account arranged them on its Kennel Builder screen, and both resources expose the `sortValue` ProPet's own Smart Feeding report sorts by, so a chart or a feeding sheet can be printed in the order the facility already sees on screen.\n\nThere is no building, area, wing or zone in the data model. A kennel belongs to exactly one kennel type and to nothing above that, so grouping by building is not something these endpoints - or ProPet itself - can express. Kennel type is the only grouping there is.\n"
        },
        {
            "name": "Products",
            "description": "Operations related to pricing rates, addons, retail products, classes, and adjustments"
        },
        {
            "name": "Webhooks",
            "description": "Manage webhook endpoints and view delivery history.\n\n**Event delivery**\nWhen a subscribed event occurs, Propetware POSTs a `WebhookEventEnvelope` JSON body to your URL. Every request includes three headers:\n- `X-Propetware-Event` \u2014 the event type string (e.g. `customer.created`)\n- `X-Propetware-Timestamp` \u2014 Unix timestamp of the delivery attempt (seconds)\n- `X-Propetware-Signature` \u2014 `sha256=<hex>` HMAC-SHA256 signature\n\n**Signature verification**\nTo verify a delivery, compute `HMAC-SHA256(webhookSecret, \"<timestamp>.<rawBody>\")` and compare the hex digest to the value of `X-Propetware-Signature` after stripping the `sha256=` prefix. Reject requests where the timestamp is more than 5 minutes old to prevent replay attacks.\n\n**Retry policy**\nFailed deliveries (non-2xx or network error) are retried up to 8 times with a 5-minute backoff, for up to 24 hours. 4xx responses are treated as permanent failures and are not retried.\n\n**Choosing what to subscribe to**\nPrefer the narrowest event that answers your question. If you need to know when pets arrive and leave, subscribe to `booking.checkedIn` and `booking.checkedOut` rather than `order.updated` \u2014 attendance writes the order too, so `order.updated` reports the same thing at much higher volume and without saying attendance was the cause.\n\nLikewise, to hear about customer-proposed changes to a reservation, subscribe to `order.changeRequested` rather than watching `order.created` for rows whose `changeRequestParentId` is set. Both fire for a change request today, but `order.created` will stop doing so.\n\nFor update events, read `changedFields` on the envelope before deciding to GET the resource. See `WebhookEventType` for the full event list and what each one means.\n"
        }
    ]
}